                <pb facs="0967" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg843"/>

                <head>No. 514.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Señor de
                            Zamacona to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Mexico</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 18,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: With much gratification this
                    legation has learned of the instructions which have been given to the governor
                    of Arizona to investigate the abuses complained of to your Department in my note
                    of the 25th of July last, to the end of procuring the punishment of the guilty
                    parties, and for maintaining, if possible, order and peace in that part of the
                    frontier. The note which under to-day’s date I address to your Department
                    concerning the recent crimes committed by organized <pb facs="0968" n="844"
                        xml:id="pg844"/> parties of evil-doers from this side of the boundary line,
                    and of which several Mexican residents of the State of Sonora have been the
                    victims, will amply show your Department how well founded are the instructions
                    given to the governor of Arizona, and how gratifying it will be if they can be
                    carried into effect.</p>
                <p>I repeat to you, Mr. Secretary, upon this occasion, the assurances of my deepest
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>M. DE ZAMACONA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
